    <statement><p>Match the following integrals with the verbal descriptions of the solids whose
volumes they give.  Put the letter of the verbal description to the left of the
corresponding integral.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_{-1}^{1}\!\!\int_{-\sqrt{1-x^{2}}}^{\sqrt{1-x^{2}}} 
	 1 - x^{2} - y^{2}\: dy dx</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_{-2}^{2}\!\!\int_{4}^{4 + \sqrt{4-x^{2}}} 
	 4x + 3y \: dy dx</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_{0}^{\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}}\!\!\int_{0}^{\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{1-3y^{2}}} 
	 \sqrt{1 -4x^{2} - 3y^{2}} \: dx dy</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{y^{2}}^{\sqrt{y}} 
	 4x^{2} + 3y^{2} \: dx dy</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2}\!\!\int_{-2}^{2} \sqrt{4 - y^{2}} \: dy dx</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
<p><ol label="A.">
<li>
<p>One eighth of an ellipsoid.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Solid under an elliptic paraboloid and over a planar region bounded by
	 two parabolas.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Solid under a plane and over one half of a circular disk.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>One half of a cylindrical rod.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Solid bounded by a circular paraboloid and a plane.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
